    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d566-a1">

                <pb facs="0536" n="524" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg524"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Chargé at Tangier</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Childs</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the French Resident General in Morocco</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Puaux</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tangier</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-09-05">September 5,
                        1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Resident General</hi>: In further reference to
                    the note which I had the honor to address to Your Excellency under date of June
                    28, 1944, setting forth the conditions under which my Government recognized as
                    exceptionally and temporarily applicable to American <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >ressortissants</hi>, wartime restrictions which have been introduced into
                    French Morocco as a result of joint action by the American and French
                    authorities in North Africa, I now have the honor to add that the measures to
                    which reference was made, as being in force at the date of that note, are
                    specified as concerning the following matters: <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>Exit visas required of American nationals on their departure from the
                            French Zone of Morocco;</item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>Measures relative to the control of exchange and currency;</item>
                        <label>3.</label>
                        <item>The requisition of crops of olives and of wheat (froment).</item>
                    </list>
                </p>
                <p>Please accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>J. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rives Childs</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
